# deploy/.env — copy from this file. docs/SELF-HOSTING.md explains each block; docs/MODELS.md the models.

# --- Required ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change-me
# Public URL of this copy (canonical links, sitemaps, share links). Build-time: rebuild the app after changing.
SITE_URL=https://records.example.org
# Where the unpacked data lives (pdf/, pages/, text/, ...). Relative to deploy/.
DATA_DIR=../data

# --- The documents (scripts/seed/sync_seed.sh) ------------------------------------------------
# Where to fetch the seed on first start: the Google Drive folder link you were given, an S3 copy
# (s3://bucket/prefix, read with the instance role) or an https:// URL. Empty = load it by hand.
SEED_URL=
# core,text = search only (~7 GB); add pages,pdf for the reader and downloads (~68 GB in all).
SEED_KINDS=core,text,pages,pdf
# Check SEED_URL for updates this often (0 = fetch once, then stop).
SEED_UPDATE_HOURS=24
# Production on AWS: also copy PDFs, page images and text to this bucket (s3://bucket[/prefix]) and
# point FILES_URL at it via CloudFront (docs/SELF-HOSTING.md section 3). FILES_S3_PRUNE_LOCAL=1
# then deletes the local copies of PDFs and page images once uploaded.
# FILES_S3=s3://my-911records-files
# FILES_S3_PRUNE_LOCAL=0
# FILES_URL=https://dxxxxxxxx.cloudfront.net   # default: the local files service

# --- Who runs this copy (shown in the footer, About, Privacy and Terms pages) -----------------
OPERATOR_NAME=Your Organisation
CONTACT_EMAIL=you@example.org
# SITE_NAME=records.example.org        # default: the host of SITE_URL
# SITE_ALIASES=www.records.example.org # hosts that redirect to SITE_URL (default www.<host>)
# ISSUES_URL=https://github.com/you/your-fork/issues   # default: off (About links CONTACT_EMAIL)
# DONATE_URL=https://...               # default: off
# Review web/app/privacy and web/app/terms: they describe 911records.org's own data practices.

# --- Databases ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Run Postgres and OpenSearch in this compose project. Remove this line to use RDS and Amazon
# OpenSearch Service instead, and fill in the block below (docs/SELF-HOSTING.md section 3).
COMPOSE_PROFILES=local-db
# PGHOST=xxxx.yyyy.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com
# PGSSLMODE=require
# DATABASE_URL=postgres://sept11:<POSTGRES_PASSWORD>@xxxx.yyyy.us-east-1.rds.amazonaws.com:5432/sept11?sslmode=no-verify
# OPENSEARCH_URL=https://search-xxxx.us-east-1.es.amazonaws.com
# OPENSEARCH_USER=admin
# OPENSEARCH_PASSWORD=...

# --- Optional ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
APP_PORT=3000
OPENSEARCH_HEAP=2g
# Analytics and ads are off for self-hosted copies; put your own GA id here to turn analytics on.
NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=off
NEXT_PUBLIC_ADS=off

# --- Search embeddings (must match the vectors in the seed: nomic-embed-text via Ollama) ------
EMBED_PROVIDER=ollama
EMBED_URL=http://ollama:11434
# EMBED_MODEL=nomic-embed-text

# --- Ask (the AI question box). Pick ONE block; leave all empty to run without Ask. -----------
# Anthropic API (the reference setup: Claude Haiku 4.5)
# LLM_PROVIDER=anthropic
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ASK_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5

# Amazon Bedrock (credentials from the instance/task role or AWS_* env vars)
# LLM_PROVIDER=bedrock
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# ASK_MODEL=us.anthropic.claude-haiku-4-5-20251001-v1:0

# OpenAI (ChatGPT models)
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# ASK_MODEL=gpt-5-mini
# ASK_PRICE_INPUT_PER_MTOK=0.25
# ASK_PRICE_OUTPUT_PER_MTOK=2

# Local / self-hosted model behind an OpenAI-compatible API (Ollama, vLLM, LM Studio, LiteLLM)
# LLM_PROVIDER=openai
# LLM_BASE_URL=http://ollama:11434/v1
# ASK_MODEL=qwen2.5:7b-instruct
# ASK_PRICE_INPUT_PER_MTOK=0
# ASK_PRICE_OUTPUT_PER_MTOK=0

# Daily spend cap for Ask in USD (estimated from the prices above; default 5)
# ASK_DAILY_USD_CAP=5
